diff --git a/research/JSRF_V22_DSOUND_INTERFACE_BOUNDARY.md b/research/JSRF_V22_DSOUND_INTERFACE_BOUNDARY.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..05e45f5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research/JSRF_V22_DSOUND_INTERFACE_BOUNDARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# JSRF v22 DirectSound interface handoff
+
+## Runtime result
+
+v22 fixed the earlier DirectSound driver failure. The title now enables the MCPX
+APU, reaches `sub_001680D0`, and that routine returns success. Startup then calls
+retail `sub_00116EC0`, which returns `0x800401F1`; the application stores that
+negative status and exits through its normal XAPI reboot path.
+
+The v22 return register is also diagnostic: `sub_00116EC0` returns with
+`ECX=0x001E3A70`. Retail `0x00116EDF` loads ECX from the vtable of the interface
+returned by the first call, so the failing second dispatch used the *primary*
+vtable at `0x001E3A70`.
+
+## Retail object layout
+
+Retail constructor `0x001693E0` installs two adjacent interface vtables:
+
+- object +0x00 -> `0x001E3A70`
+- object +0x04 -> `0x001E3A5C`
+
+The relevant slots are:
+
+- `0x001E3A70 + 0x00 -> 0x00168310` (root QueryInterface-style method)
+- `0x001E3A70 + 0x0C -> 0x00168480` (root initialization method)
+- `0x001E3A5C + 0x0C -> 0x00168400` (secondary-interface method)
+
+`sub_00116EC0` asks the root object for GUID
+`588211C6-F18C-11D2-8D16-00105A6B7166`. In retail `0x00168310`, that exact IID
+returns `this + 4`, whose vtable is `0x001E3A5C`. It then asks that secondary
+interface for `C50A7E93-F395-4834-9EF6-7FA99DE50966` (`IID_IDirectSound8`) via
+slot +0x0C.
+
+The primary slot +0x0C (`0x00168480`) returns `0x800401F1` if object+0x14 is
+already initialized. That is exactly the v22 result and is consistent with the
+second call dispatching through `0x001E3A70` instead of the required secondary
+vtable.
+
+## Boundary evidence
+
+All three relevant methods are vtable-only and have explicit standalone retail
+boundaries separated by alignment padding:
+
+- `0x00168310..0x001683F8`, final `ret 0x0C`, next code at `0x00168400`
+- `0x00168400..0x00168472`, final `ret 0x0C`, next code at `0x00168480`
+- `0x00168480..0x001684DE`, final `ret 0x08`
+
+They have no direct CALL xrefs. This is the same class of boundary evidence as
+earlier JSRF vtable-only fixes: the generic detector can otherwise weaken a
+runtime seed into an alias and preserve the wrong surrounding body/entry
+semantics.
+
+## v23 action
+
+v23 therefore does not force any HRESULT or replace DirectSound behavior. It
+pins these three retail-proven methods as standalone functions, seeds them as
+runtime vtable entries, and adds function-level tracing for the next Windows
+run. If the boundary correction is causal, `sub_00116EC0` should reach the
+secondary slot `0x00168400` and no longer return the primary-interface
+`0x800401F1` state error. If not, the added trace identifies the exact remaining
+translation mismatch without altering guest state.
